Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Exercise (2.4)", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.999754578971438*^9, 3.999754602697837*^9}, {
  3.999754864261216*^9, 
  3.999754865435939*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ca0f8e9f-ad6b-4ae2-8bde-\
a9115b9a28fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let E be the elliptic curve ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["y", "2"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cf8db4a-9991-4a6d-b67e-93cabd6539be"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "3"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "b3112997-9619-40c1-8fe5-8c566a31dbe1"],
 " \[Minus] 34x + 37 de\[FiLigature]ned over Q. Let P = (1, 2) and Q = (6, \
7).\n(a) Compute P + Q.\n(b) Note that P \[Congruent] Q (mod 5). Compute 2P \
on E mod 5. Show that\nthe answer is the same as (P +Q) mod 5. Observe that \
since P \[Congruent] Q,\nthe formula for adding the points mod 5 is not the \
reduction of the\nformula for adding P +Q. However, the answers are the \
same."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.999754519974433*^9, 3.999754561742778*^9}, {
  3.999754606450465*^9, 
  3.999754607145917*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e41413cf-fd9b-4f60-b4f5-\
c81253dfd3e9"],

